  "body": "Codex's `web_search = \"cached\"` reaches the ChatGPT backend unchanged for Codex's own models: the request carries `{\"type\":\"web_search\",\"external_web_access\":false}` and magpie forwards it.\n\nFor a model that can't search (a third-party model run in Codex), magpie runs the search itself (`webSearch` in internal/gateway/search.go). The client's tool is read only as a yes/no (`r.WebSearch` in responses.go), so `external_web_access:false` is dropped. The searcher's request is sent as Anthropic `web_search_20250305` and, to a Codex or OpenAI searcher, translated to a plain `{\"type\":\"web_search\"}` (responses.go, near line 1529), which searches live. A user who chose cached gets live search on these turns.\n\nAsked about by lucy_85908 on Discord (#feedback, v0.1.2682). Seen while fixing the searcher's model pick (gpt-6.1-sol instead of the account's cheap model).\n\nWhat a fix would do: carry the client's `external_web_access` from the turn into the search, and send it to an OpenAI/Codex searcher. Claude, Gemini and the search APIs have no cached-only mode, so the setting can only reach an OpenAI searcher. The quota a search spends is mostly the searcher model's tokens, so cached would not save much. The point is to respect what the user chose.\n",
  "closed_by": null,
