   "created_at": "2026-11-08T21:32:06Z",
   "updated_at": "2026-11-08T21:32:06Z",
   "body": "A fix is on [the fork branch](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/5018-cached-search-model-wire), commit [042f814a9](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/042f814a9a3c96a9704cf097793088d8944100f0), based on `ed0ab567`.\n\nThe client's `external_web_access` now survives the internal Messages search request and reaches a Responses search model. Explicit `false`, `true`, and absence stay distinct. This uses the existing `Request.WebAccess` and search context; native Responses passthrough stays covered. Providers/search APIs without a cached-only option do not gain one.\n\nAn actual local HTTP gateway with a target that cannot search and a fake Codex Responses search model observes the outgoing search tool. On the base, both explicit values were dropped; after the fix all three cases pass. Parent verification passed that regression and existing direct Codex/native passthrough checks under `-race`; gateway vet, formatting and the full `nogui` build passed. No live vendor, full suite or cross-platform runtime was tested. AI-assisted implementation and review.",
